From: ai-hakzarov <226896199+ai-hakzarov@users.noreply.github.com>
Date: Wed, 7 Oct 2026 23:02:48 -0400
Subject: [PATCH] 9745: Decompiler: lane split reassembles a value consumed
 whole by a call

LaneDivide::traceForward refused any CALL, CALLIND, CALLOTHER or RETURN that
took the traced value as an input, so a vector built or used lane by lane and
then passed by value to a function (or to a user-defined op such as a byte
shuffle) kept the whole-register variable and printed as byte pieces. Such an
op is now a terminal: the lanes are concatenated back with PIECE ops placed
before it and the op's inputs are reattached with the reassembled value; an op
that takes the value in more than one slot is reattached once. A value that is
already such a reassembly (defined by a PIECE and read only by the consuming
op) is left alone, so the division cannot feed itself if it runs more than
once. A datatest compiled from a few lines of C covers a vector scaled lane by
lane, stored, and handed whole to PSHUFB.
---
